#30201
Southwest Meadow~
A wide meadow of tall grass and wildflowers fills the far southwest corner
of the land, hemmed in by brown rock to the south and west. Bees drone
among the blossoms, and a strange whirring like a spinning top rises and
fades on the wind. It is a quiet, forgotten place, and the only path leads
east.
