#30202
Woodland Rock Face~
Trees crowd against a wall of brown rock that marks the southern edge of
the land, their roots clinging to every crack. One stretch of the rock face
is fractured and crumbling, a web of fine cracks spreading from its center
as if a sharp blast might open it. Paths lead north, east and west through
the woods.
