#30203
Southern Woods~
Old trees stand in loose rows along the southern edge of the land, their
branches meeting overhead in a leafy roof. The ground is churned by heavy,
clawed feet and littered with snapped twigs and gnawed bones. Somewhere off
among the trunks a twig cracks. Paths lead north, east and west.
