#30212
Leever Dunes~
Low dunes of pale sand roll along the southern edge of the land, shifting
and hissing whenever the wind picks up. Little whorls in the sand mark
where something has burrowed down out of sight. A cracked face of rock
rises at one side, as though a blast might open it. Paths lead east and
west.
