#30214
Southeast Grassland~
Wide grassland sweeps toward the southeastern coast, the long grass bent
flat by a constant wind that carries salt from the sea. Small round stones
lie scattered about, some half buried as if spat with force. Gulls cry
somewhere to the east. Paths lead east toward the shore and west across the
grass.
