#30216
Western Meadow Edge~
Open meadow runs right up to the western edge of the land, where the grass
stops at a sheer brown bluff. A strange rising whirr comes and goes on the
wind, and deep, heavy hoofprints cut through the flowers as if something
large and four-legged patrols here. Paths lead north toward the rocks and
east into the woods.
