#30218
Old Forest Clearing~
A hushed clearing opens among ancient oaks, their bark gnarled and split
with age and their roots heaving up the soil. Fallen leaves lie ankle deep
and smell of rain. At one edge a single bush has withered to a dry, papery
brown, oddly lifeless beside the green. Trails wander away in every
direction.
