The Old Man's Cave~
A low cave opens into the hillside, its walls black with the soot of two
fires that never seem to burn down. The flames stand an equal distance
apart, and the bare floor between them has been swept clean, as though
someone has been waiting a long time for a visitor. It is dangerous out
there, and this is the place that knows it.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
cave opening~
0 0 30200
S
#30651
The White Sword Cave~
Spray from the waterfall drifts in at the mouth of this cave and beads on
the rock. Two fires burn in shallow pits against the far wall, throwing a
steady light across a floor scored by the boots of the few who climbed this
high. The stone here is pale and clean, as if the mountain itself were
holding something worth keeping.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
cave opening~
0 0 30322
S
#30652
Beneath the Hero's Grave~
A narrow stair beneath the old headstone ends in a cold, close vault. Twin
fires burn on either side of a worn stone plinth, and their light does not
reach the corners. The air smells of earth and iron, and the silence has
the weight of a promise made to whoever proved strong enough to come down
here.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
push opening~
4 0 30281
S
#30653
The Hermit's Cave~
This cave sits high in the northeastern rocks where few travellers think to
look. Two small fires warm a dry floor, and a writing desk has been made
from a flat slab of stone. Whoever lives here keeps the place tidy and
keeps to the old courtesies; the royal family's seal would be known here at
a glance.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
cave opening~
0 0 30326
S
#30654
A Hidden Heart Grotto~
Rubble from the shattered wall lies across the mouth of this little grotto.
Beyond it the cave is dry and quiet, lit by two steady fires set into the
floor. Something warm and red glows on a ledge between them, a gift left
for anyone determined enough to blast their way in.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
bomb opening~
4 0 30211
S
#30655
A Grotto in the Mountain~
The blast that opened this cave left its walls raw and sharp, and dust
still hangs in the firelight. The chamber beyond is small and surprisingly
warm, sheltered from the wind that scours the mountain outside. A faint red
pulse of light comes from the far end, steady as a heartbeat.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
bomb opening~
4 0 30292
S
#30656
Beneath the Burned Bush~
Ash from the burned bush has drifted down the steps into this hollow under
the roots. Two fires burn here already, older than the one that opened the
way, and the earthen walls are hung with pale threads of root. The place
feels like a secret the forest kept for itself.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
burn opening~
4 0 30255
S
#30657
The Raft Island~
A spit of sand and rock stands alone in open water, reachable only by raft
from the dock on the shore. Waves lap at every side, and a single scrubby
tree leans over a sheltered hollow in the middle. It is the kind of place a
reward would be hidden: obvious from the shore and impossible to reach
without the means.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
~
0 0 30295
S
#30658
Across the Narrow Water~
This rocky ledge lies just beyond a channel of water too wide to step and
too narrow to bother swimming. A traveller with a stepladder can bridge it
in a moment. The ledge is quiet, sheltered from the coast wind by a
shoulder of rock, and littered with gull feathers and driftwood.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
~
0 0 30247
S
#30659
Hollow of the Old Tree~
The burned bush opened onto a hollow beneath the roots of an enormous old
tree. The walls are packed earth and root, and the light here is strange:
it seems to come from somewhere other than Hyrule. A soft hum fills the
hollow, and the air carries a faint smell of dust, coins and arcade lights.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
burn opening~
4 0 30220
S
#30660
It's a Secret to Everybody~
The burned bush revealed a short stair down into a cosy earthen cave. Two
fires crackle in the gloom, and the floor between them is scuffed by heavy,
clawed feet. Whoever lives here is generous with strangers, provided the
strangers keep quiet about where they found the money.
~
0 AD 11
D4
~
burn rupee grotto~
4 0 30233
S
#30661
It's a Secret to Everybody~
Broken stone from the bombed wall lies just inside this cramped cave. Two
fires burn in the dark, and their light catches a few loose glints on the
floor. The place has the cheerful untidiness of someone who hides coin for
a living and expects to be found now and then.
~
